**One last honest thing I want to say.** I built exactly what you asked for, and I've tried to make every layer of it honest with you about its limitations. The hard rails will protect you from catastrophic loss. The paper-trade mode will tell you if the strategy works *for you* before you risk anything. The attribution will tell you *why* it works or doesn't. But the underlying strategy class — ATM/OTM options scalping with 10-15 min holds on ₹15K capital — is genuinely difficult, and most people who attempt it lose money. The system I built can't change that math. What it *can* do is make sure you find out before losing a lot, and make sure that when you do find out, you have the data to understand what happened.

If after 5-10 paper sessions the numbers look bad, please trust the data and stop. Don't optimize indicators to fit history; that's overfitting and it will lose live. The honest thing the system is telling you at that point is: this strategy doesn't have edge for you at this capital. That's a valid answer.

